    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "O’Mahony Walsh & Associates Ltd are delighted to present this impressively spacious \r\nfive-bedroom bungalow, ideally located in Aherla village, Co. Cork. Set on 0.3 of an acre, it offers the perfect the perfect balance of peaceful countryside living and everyday convenience, this property will appeal to those seeking tranquillity without compromising on accessibility to local amenities.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 164 sq.m., the accommodation is bright, well-proportioned and thoughtfully laid out, providing generous living space throughout. The beautifully maintained rear and side gardens create an inviting outdoor setting, ideal for relaxation and al fresco dining.\r\n\r\nConveniently situated just 15 minutes from Ballincollig and 20 minutes from Macroom, this is a superb opportunity to acquire a comfortable home in a highly accessible yet scenic location. Early viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "O’Mahony Walsh & Associates Ltd are delighted to present this impressively spacious\r\nfive-bedroom bungalow, ideally located in Aherla village, Co. Cork. Set on 0.3 of an acre, it offers the perfect the perfect balance of peaceful countryside living and everyday convenience, this property will appeal to those seeking tranquillity without compromising on accessibility to local amenities.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 164 sq.m., the accommodation is bright, well-proportioned and thoughtfully laid out, providing generous living space throughout. The beautifully maintained rear and side gardens create an inviting outdoor setting, ideal for relaxation and al fresco dining.\r\n\r\nConveniently situated just 15 minutes from Ballincollig and 20 minutes from Macroom, this is a superb opportunity to acquire a comfortable home in a highly accessible yet scenic location. Early viewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nFoyer & Hallway – 2.72 X 2.02 & 13.87 X 1.44m\r\nAn enclosed porch opens into a bright and inviting entrance hallway, complete with practical tiled flooring and providing access to all accommodation.\r\n\r\nLiving Room– 5.32m x 3.36m\r\nA comfortable living room enjoys a pleasant front aspect, with large windows allowing for an abundance of natural light. A wood-burning stove and soft carpet flooring combine to create a warm and inviting atmosphere.\r\n\r\nDining Room & Conservatory – 3.87m x 2.99m & 3.86m x 3.70m\r\nAccessed via an archway from both the living room and the kitchen, this impressive dining room serves as a central hub for entertaining and family gatherings. Feature French doors provide seamless access to the sunroom and rear garden, enhancing the sense of space and light.\r\n\r\nKitchen – 3.86m x 2.99m\r\nA spacious galley-style kitchen enjoys a rear aspect window overlooking the garden. Plenty of natural light. Finished with tiled flooring and light grey painted oak cabinetry, it offers ample storage and generous counter space, while a breakfast bar provides a convenient additional seating area.\r\n\r\nUtility – 2.98m 2.52m\r\nThis well-proportioned utility room has tiled flooring and a rear access frosted door to the garden. Recess for tall refrigerator/storage and plumbed for washing machine. Folding counter with sink and cabinets provide ample storage.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom – 4.50m x 3.80m\r\nSpacious double bedroom with timber flooring and patio doors to side garden. Built in wardrobes provide ample storage space. Tiled En-Suite bathroom with enclosed electric shower, W.H.B & W.C.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 4.21m x 2.99m\r\nA well-appointed double bedroom with timber flooring, large wardrobes and front aspect window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 - 4.00m x 2.99m\r\nBright and inviting double bedroom with timber flooring, large wardrobes & rear aspect window.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 - 3.80m x 2.99m\r\nComfortable double bedroom with timber flooring, built in slide robes, rear aspect window. En-Suite complete with enclosed electric shower, W.H.B & W.C.\r\n\r\nBedroom 5 - 3.32m x 2.99m\r\nCurrently used as an office, this bright room has timber flooring and a front aspect window. Ample room for a double bed.\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom – 2.99m x 2.66m\r\nLarge main bathroom with soaking tub/shower combination, tiled flooring and wall with W.H.B and W.C. Front aspect window.\r\n\r\nGARDEN DETAILS\r\nA beautifully landscaped South and West-facing rear garden features meticulously maintained lawns, vibrant flower beds, mature fruit trees, and carefully curated shrubs, creating a private and truly picturesque outdoor space.\r\nA thoughtfully designed patio area, finished with a blend of gravel and stone tiles provides the perfect setting for relaxing or entertaining in the sun.\r\nThe property also benefits from a Steeltech shed measuring approximately 3.20m x 3.20m, along with a dog run located adjacent, measuring approximately 3.15m x 2.20m, and a glasshouse measuring 8’ x 6’ (2.45m x 1.82m)."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tImpressive five-bedroom bungalow \r\n•\tB3 Rated\r\n•\tSpacious accommodation extending to approx. 164 sq.m. \r\n•\tBright, well-proportioned and thoughtfully designed layout \r\n•\tBeautifully maintained rear and side gardens \r\n•\tIdeal outdoor areas for relaxation and al fresco dining \r\n•\tLocated in Aherla village \r\n•\tExcellent balance of tranquillity and accessibility\r\n•\tConvenient access to Ballincollig (15 minutes) and Macroom (20 minutes)\r\n•\tMinutes’ walk from Centra & two pubs. \r\n•\tHeat Recovery and Ventilation (Mechanical Ventilation) system built into the house."
      },
